<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jiroft</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jiroft is a city in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kerman">Kerman</a> province in south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, in the Halil river valley. From 2001 looting near the town revealed the Jiroft culture of the 3rd millennium BCE, with large settlements such as Konar Sandal and finely carved chlorite vessels, some of which reached <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a>. Some scholars identify the region with the land of Marhashi or <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aratta">Aratta</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jiroft.jpg" alt="Jiroft" width="320" height="245" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Aryan1900 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:IMaryan20190409_174513.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
